<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hotula Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Khutula Khan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hotula Khan was a khan of the Khamag Mongol confederation in the mid-12th century, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khabul-khan">Khabul Khan</a> and uncle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yesugei">Yesügei</a>. Elected after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatars</a> handed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambaghai">Ambaghai Khan</a> to the Jin, he waged wars of revenge against the Tatars. After him the khanship lapsed until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Temüjin</a>, the future Genghis Khan, revived it.</p></div>
